# Job activation flags for .github/workflows/lean.yml.
#
# These began as milestone gates for the Lean port and now serve as a kill
# switch for a gate that has grown too expensive to run on every PR.
#
# LEAN_SELFHOST gates the Level 1 sweep. LEAN_SELFHOST_L2 gates the Level 2
# (metacircular) sweep separately. It was OFF because L2 took ~16 minutes of a
# CI run we want to keep under 10, the Zig backend being ~7.5x slower per case
# than the Chez Scheme path it replaced (#385).
#
# Back ON: L2 is now ~5x rather than ~7.5x (measured serially on an M-series
# Mac, 154s vs 31s on Fib; slowest of the five cases 177s), so the budgets
# raised in #384 are lowered back to their pre-#384 values in the same change --
# L2 CASE_TIMEOUT 1200 -> 600 and lean-selfhost timeout-minutes 90 -> 60. That
# is exactly what #385 names as its completion criterion.
#
# The numbers above are local. CI hardware is slower, so this run is also the
# experiment: if the job does not fit, the honest response is to flip this back
# to 0 rather than to raise the budgets again. Re-measure at any time with
# `mise run perf-baseline -- --tier=l2-ratio`, which needs the Chez control that
# #400 removes.
LEAN_ZIG=1
LEAN_SELFHOST=1
LEAN_SELFHOST_L2=1
